# `PreparedProtocol`

<SymbolMeta />
<SymbolSignature />

`PreparedProtocol` is the immutable hand-off between application validation and runtime construction. Its value is retained by the prepared application and is the authoritative place for validated routes, selected codecs, scope-aware dispatch plans, and stable tooling facts.

## Build contract

`build(self, runtime: &AppRuntime)` runs only after the root DI container exists. Use it to create `Runtime`, the protocol's dispatch or serve layer. It may wire resolvers, routers, codecs, and transport-facing handles that depend on the validated application runtime.

Do not repeat descriptor or scope-topology validation in `build`; those concerns are complete before this point. Do not start the endpoint loop here either. Endpoint work begins when the resulting runtime is passed to [`Serve`](./Serve).

## Tooling contract

`tooling` reports stable protocol-owned metadata retained by prepared state. It must not require a live listener, connection, task, or endpoint. This keeps tooling deterministic and available before serving begins.

The associated `Runtime` type implements [`ProtocolRuntime`](./ProtocolRuntime). See [the custom protocol guide](/docs/latest/framework/extensions/protocol-authoring) for the full definition-to-runtime lifecycle.

